# From https://www.oddsbusters.com/us/getting-started/strategies/blackjack/blackjack-cheat-sheet/
#
# This is for a 4-8 hand deck where dealer stands on soft 17
#
# The first 3 columns represent the player's hand
# - if the first column is empty, then the 2nd and 3rd column represents the player cards
# - else if there is a number in the first column it represents the total sum of the player hand
#
#        Dealer's Card
#  ----------------------------
#  2  3  4  5  6  7  8  9  10 A

# For split, the first column represents the pair of cards
[split]
2  PH PH P  P  P  P  H  H  H  H
3  PH PH P  P  P  P  H  H  H  H
4  H  H  H  PH PH H  H  H  H  H
5  DH DH DH DH DH DH DH DH H  H
6  PH P  P  P  P  H  H  H  H  H
7  P  P  P  P  P  P  H  H  H  H
8  P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P
9  P  P  P  P  P  S  P  P  S  S
10 S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S
11 P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P  P

# For soft, first column represents the total value of player hand with all aces counting as one
[soft]
3  H  H  H  DH DH H  H  H  H  H
4  H  H  H  DH DH H  H  H  H  H
5  H  H  DH DH DH H  H  H  H  H
6  H  H  DH DH DH H  H  H  H  H
7  H  DH DH DH DH H  H  H  H  H
8  S  DS DS DS DS S  S  H  H  H
9  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S
10 S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S
11 S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S  S

# For hard, first column represents the total value of player hand
[hard]
4  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H
5  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H
6  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H  H
